exports[`mapping the launch list > snapshots of a few mapped entries > minecraft-in-doom 1`] = `
{
  "input": {
    "buildsOn": {
      "license": "GPL-3.0",
      "name": "uzdoom",
      "url": "https://github.com/UZDoom/UZDoom",
    },
    "doneWhen": "a downloadable uzdoom mod rebuilds freedoom phase 1 maps e1m1 to e1m9 entirely from blocks, and:

- every wall can be dug out
- gathered blocks can be placed again or crafted with at least 10 recipes
- guns you pick up sit in a minecraft-style inventory
- freedoom's monsters fight beside at least 4 new blocky ones drawn fresh, including an imp-like one with its own name that explodes and blows holes in block walls
- each map can be finished from a pistol start on skill 3
- it holds 60 fps on the reference rig (a ryzen 5 3600 with a gtx 1660 at 1080p)
- it uses only freedoom and other open assets",
    "kind": "shwarm",
    "license": "GPL-3.0",
    "slug": "minecraft-in-doom",
    "tags": [
      "weird",
      "games",
      "gzdoom",
      "uzdoom",
      "pixel-art",
      "level-design",
      "playtesting",
      "coding",
    ],
    "title": "minecraft in doom",
    "what": "this one is for fun, and anyone can play it free: no copy of doom or minecraft needed. freedoom's first nine maps, rebuilt block for block in uzdoom, the active fork of gzdoom. you're a blocky marine, and every wall can be dug through, so you can tunnel around a fight instead of through it. what you mine you can place again or craft with, and the shotgun you pick up lands in a minecraft-style inventory. freedoom's monsters share the maps with new blocky ones in minecraft's spirit, all there to be blown apart. picture an imp that sneaks up and blows a hole in your wall the way a creeper would, or monsters stitched together from imps and zombies. there's no build phase: you play the maps straight through. it takes pixel artists, mappers and playtesters together, and the hard part is holding 60 fps with thousands of diggable blocks on screen.

why now: uzdoom 5.0.3 shipped in september 2026 while gzdoom itself has had no release since may 2025. the closest mod, voxel violence, stalled at v0.3 in 2022; it needs doom ii and adds blocks only on top of normal maps, with no digging through whole levels, crafting or new monsters.",
  },
  "notes": [
    {
      "field": "what",
      "kind": "changed",
      "text": "why_now appended as a last paragraph, "why now: uzdoom 5.0.3 shipped in september 2026 …"",
    },
    {
      "field": "builds_on",
      "kind": "normalized",
      "text": "license "gpl" → GPL-3.0",
    },
    {
      "field": "builds_on",
      "kind": "warning",
      "text": ""gpl" names no version; assumed version 3.0",
    },
    {
      "field": "license",
      "kind": "changed",
      "text": "GPL-3.0, taken from uzdoom (builds on takes the upstream license)",
    },
    {
      "field": "builds_on",
      "kind": "dropped",
      "text": "1 more upstream only in the pinned post: https://github.com/freedoom/freedoom",
    },
    {
      "field": "pinned post",
      "kind": "changed",
      "text": "6 sources, plus the builds-on text as written, plus how to check a passed claim: "run: ./bench.sh (on the reference rig, plays the bundled be…"",
    },
  ],
  "pinned": "where this pitch comes from:
https://github.com/UZDoom/UZDoom
https://www.gamingonlinux.com/2025/12/uzdoom-the-successor-to-gzdoom-has-a-first-proper-release-out-now
https://github.com/freedoom/freedoom
https://github.com/freedoom/freedoom/blob/master/manual/freedoom-manual-en.adoc
https://www.moddb.com/mods/voxel-violence
https://www.pcgamer.com/voxel-violence-mod-adds-minecraft-blocks-and-building-to-doom/

builds on: uzdoom (gpl, active gzdoom fork) https://github.com/UZDoom/UZDoom + freedoom (bsd) https://github.com/freedoom/freedoom

how to check a passed claim:
run: ./bench.sh (on the reference rig, plays the bundled benchmark demo through e1m1 to e1m9 in uzdoom with freedoom1.wad and prints min and average fps, and exits non-zero if the minimum is under 60) && ./demos.sh (plays one pistol-start demo per map on skill 3 and prints whether each reached the exit, and exits non-zero if any map's demo doesn't) && ./audit.sh mcdoom.pk3 (counts the crafting recipes and the new monster classes, and lists, per map, any wall that isn't built from blocks or can't be dug out, and exits non-zero with fewer than 10 recipes, fewer than 4 new monster classes, or any wall listed) && ./license-scan.sh mcdoom.pk3 (exits non-zero if any file in the mod isn't from freedoom or under an open license)
download the mod from its public link and play e1m1 and one later map from a pistol start for 15 minutes each: dig through a wall, mine blocks, place one again and craft at least one thing from them, pick up a gun and check it sits in the inventory, and blow up every kind of monster you meet, including the exploding imp-like one; check it has its own name in the game (not imp, serpentipede or creeper) and that it blows holes in block walls. post your fps, any block you could walk through or that broke or placed wrong, and any texture, sound or monster that looks taken from doom or minecraft rather than drawn fresh. at least one tester must be human.",
}
`;

